The package degorasasi provides CMake targets:

    find_package(DegorasASI CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Degoras::ASI)

Runtime requirement: this library controls ZWO ASI astronomy cameras and depends on the proprietary ZWO ASI Camera
SDK. The ASICamera2 runtime library must be discoverable at run time (install the ZWO driver package, or keep
ASICamera2.dll / libASICamera2.so on PATH / LD_LIBRARY_PATH / next to your executable).

ABI note: the public API passes C++ standard-library types across the library boundary, so consumers MUST use a
toolchain and standard-library implementation compatible with the one the library was built with. This constrains
LINKAGE, not platform: the library itself carries no platform lock, and MinGW/UCRT64 on Windows is the reference
(validated) toolchain.

Static builds only: the ASI import library must also be locatable at link time. Set ASI_SDK_ROOT (CMake or
environment variable) to the SDK root if it is not auto-detected.
